~ Generic NIR LED, a placeholder until a real part is chosen. Every value below is an assumption. To use a real part, write a design file named for it that starts with `design led`.

Peak wavelength: lam = 850 :nm

    ~ Design choice. It must sit where the sensor still has useful quantum efficiency.

Radiant flux: Phi = 0.5 :W

    ~ Assumed output of one LED at its rated current. Take it from the datasheet.

Wall-plug efficiency (0, 1): eta = 0.3 | 0.4

    ~ Assumed optical power out over electrical power in. Take it from the datasheet.

Beam half-angle (0, 90): theta = 15 :deg

    ~ Assumed for a 30 degree full-angle optic. Take it from the datasheet.

Mass: m = 1 :g

    ~ Assumed.
